name=FSR-UPSC (ZombieBuddy)
id=FSR_UPSC_ZB
modversion=1.1.0
versionMin=42.22
versionMax=42.22
author=kawatarenosora
require=\ZombieBuddy
javaJarFile=media/java/fsr-upsc-agent.jar
javaPkgName=fsrupsc
description=AMD FidelityFX (FSR) upscaling for Project Zomboid B42, ZombieBuddy edition: no -javaagent launch option is needed, the ZombieBuddy mod loads the agent jar (release 2.x or BETA 3.x both work). World pass renders at a reduced resolution (FidelityFX quality presets) and is resolved with FSR 1 EASU+RCAS, or FSR 2 / FSR 3.1 temporal upscaling (GL compute) with injected sub-pixel camera jitter, depth chain, auto-reactive masks and entity motion vectors, plus optional software frame generation on the present path (FsrControl.fsr2FgTest). Falls back to FSR 1 automatically on any compute fault. First launch shows a ZombieBuddy approval dialog for the agent jar, choose persist. Built for B42.22 (revision e013dbb529) only: the mod list version gate (versionMin/versionMax) blocks enabling on other builds, and a same-label hotfix would run stock instead of transforming. Do not enable together with the javaagent edition (mod id FSR_UPSC) - one of the two must stay off.

The agent jar ships inside this mod folder: media\java\fsr-upsc-agent.jar.
ZombieBuddy loads it from mod.info (javaJarFile/javaPkgName) on game start;
hook groups, downscale and upscaler settings behave exactly like the
javaagent edition (ModOptions.ini / fsrupsc.FsrControl from Lua).
